{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MAX = 510;\nint n, m, mod;\nint binom[MAX][MAX], f1[MAX], f2[MAX][MAX], g1[MAX], g2[MAX][MAX];\n\nvoid precompute_binom() {\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        binom[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j)\n            binom[i][j] = (binom[i-1][j-1] + binom[i-1][j]) % mod;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid compute_f1_g1() {\n    f1[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        long long sum_f = 0, sum_g = 0;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n            long long a = 1LL * f1[j-1] * f1[i-j] % mod;\n            sum_f = (sum_f + a * binom[i-1][j-1]) % mod;\n            long long t = (1LL * f1[j-1] * g1[i-j] + 1LL * g1[j-1] * f1[i-j]) % mod;\n            t = t * (i+1) % mod;\n            long long b = (a * (binom[j][2] + binom[i-j+1][2]) % mod + t) % mod;\n            sum_g = (sum_g + b * binom[i-1][j-1]) % mod;\n        }\n        f1[i] = 1LL * (i+1) * sum_f % mod;\n        g1[i] = sum_g;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid compute_f2_g2() {\n    f2[0][0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= min(i, m); ++j) {\n            f2[i][j] = f2[i-1][j];\n            g2[i][j] = g2[i-1][j];\n            for (int k = 1; k <= j; ++k) {\n                long long base_f = (i - k) ? f2[i-k-1][j-k] : 1;\n                long long base_g = (i - k) ? g2[i-k-1][j-k] : 0;\n                f2[i][j] = (f2[i][j] + base_f * f1[k] % mod * binom[j][k]) % mod;\n                g2[i][j] = (g2[i][j] + (base_f * g1[k] + base_g * f1[k]) % mod * binom[j][k]) % mod;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &n, &m, &mod);\n    precompute_binom();\n    compute_f1_g1();\n    compute_f2_g2();\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", g2[n][m]);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    mod = int(data[2])\n\n    MAX = n + 5  # enough for n up to 500\n    binom = [[0] * (MAX) for _ in range(MAX)]\n    f1 = [0] * (MAX)\n    g1 = [0] * (MAX)\n    f2 = [[0] * (MAX) for _ in range(MAX)]\n    g2 = [[0] * (MAX) for _ in range(MAX)]\n\n    # precompute binom\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        binom[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            binom[i][j] = (binom[i-1][j-1] + binom[i-1][j]) % mod\n\n    # compute f1 and g1\n    f1[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        sum_f = 0\n        sum_g = 0\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            a = (f1[j-1] * f1[i-j]) % mod\n            sum_f = (sum_f + a * binom[i-1][j-1]) % mod\n            t = (f1[j-1] * g1[i-j] + g1[j-1] * f1[i-j]) % mod\n            t = (t * (i + 1)) % mod\n            b = (a * (binom[j][2] + binom[i-j+1][2]) % mod + t) % mod\n            sum_g = (sum_g + b * binom[i-1][j-1]) % mod\n        f1[i] = ((i + 1) * sum_f) % mod\n        g1[i] = sum_g\n\n    # compute f2 and g2\n    f2[0][0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(0, min(i, m) + 1):\n            f2[i][j] = f2[i-1][j]\n            g2[i][j] = g2[i-1][j]\n            for k in range(1, j + 1):\n                base_f = f2[i-k-1][j-k] if (i - k) else 1\n                base_g = g2[i-k-1][j-k] if (i - k) else 0\n                f2[i][j] = (f2[i][j] + base_f * f1[k] % mod * binom[j][k]) % mod\n                g2[i][j] = (g2[i][j] + (base_f * g1[k] + base_g * f1[k]) % mod * binom[j][k]) % mod\n\n    print(g2[n][m] % mod)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0967351421713829, -0.00910948310047388, -1.4185804502631072e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -0.000556314189452678, -1.1801649634435307e-05, 0.0, -0.000722266617231071, -0.024057263508439064, -0.5043913722038269, -0.3875062167644501, -8.34461570775602e-06, -0.0039109899662435055, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00020454221521504223, 0.0, -0.0007160721579566598, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.023246029391884804, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -2.1576648578047752e-05, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, -0.0011701886542141438, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -0.0017113338690251112, -0.5759655833244324, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.16026045382022858, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0002203936892328784, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.8954096958623268e-05, 0.0, -0.0015163839561864734, -0.0012740122620016336, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.5759533643722534, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.05398175120353699, -6.496695277746767e-05, -0.4886404871940613, -0.0009173714206553996, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -0.13996051251888275, -0.10311711579561234, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.9739660024642944, -0.9459659457206726, -0.9994598627090454, -0.2813704013824463, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0038194339722394943, -0.4205872118473053, -0.3421896398